{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "sol",
      "decision": "reuse",
      "ability": "navigate",
      "reason": "This is the existing navigation function: paid movement toward a chosen destination through observed, physically traversable space. It needs routing diagnosis and potentially a corrective implementation, not a separately learned ability. The shelter has a declared doorway, but Lin's position near its approach could constrain passage. The supplied observations do not establish whether a collision-free route exists; neither a routing defect nor a completely blocked exit should be assumed.",
      "specification": "Use the current-conversation implementation handoff to inspect and, where necessary, repair kernel.navigate while preserving its interface ID, mastery, prerequisites and public parameters: {target:string(maxLength 1000),x:number,y:number}, all required, no additional properties. Reproduce departure from the observed shelter interior using the actual requested destination; do not invent a replacement destination. Transform the shelter's 2x2 footprint, 0.1 walls and width-1 doorway by its actual pose. Use authoritative actor radii and the same shared geometry for planning, swept movement collision and interaction reach. Treat walls as collision segments with a real doorway opening, not the whole reserved footprint as an impassable solid. Include Lin and other actual occupants as dynamic obstacles without moving them or assuming cooperation. Generate clearance-valid interior, doorway and exterior connections with a local visibility graph or equivalent bounded continuous-space search; validate every connection against inflated obstacles and sweep-check every executed movement. Distinguish a proven clearance obstruction from exhausted search or insufficient observed terrain. Revalidate occupancy each movement round and replan within the existing computation budget; fail safely when passage cannot be established. Retain route progress and the observed-geometry revision, invalidating stale plans when relevant geometry or occupancy changes. Preserve speed 0.8, actual-distance energy charges including carried mass, normal elapsed rounds, metabolism and exposure; no teleportation, free recovery, wall passage or shelter modification. Cancel pending navigation on death or incompatible interruption without subsequent movement or charges; there is no material escrow. Emit existing moved, arrived and failed events, with failed data carrying a structured diagnostic code, observed blocker IDs where established, attempted doorway and measured clearance where available. Do not expose unobserved obstacles. Version the routing correction, preserve source history, and migrate by invalidating cached routes only: retain positions, objects, inventory, mastery and wellbeing. Add regression tests for clear exits, partially and fully obstructed doorways, rotated shelters, actor clearance, dynamic occupants and death cancellation. Development and review advance no simulation time.",
      "experienceReview": "The review, diagnosis and routing correction are not performed experiences and award no happiness. Ordinary successful navigation is instrumental movement, not by itself evidence of enjoyment or relief from distress; no new mental source is justified by these records. Actual movement continues to affect energy, exposure and physical comfort normally. Preserve the existing thermal-refuge rule and its shelter-comfort-qualified and warming-comfort-qualified subscriptions without duplicating it or awarding it merely for departure.",
      "visualReview": "Render the shelter walls and doorway from the same transformed geometry used by collision and routing. Show any route preview only along validated traversable segments. Bind movement and arrival feedback to moved and arrived; bind obstruction feedback to failed, distinguishing an observed occupied passage, insufficient clearance, unknown terrain and search failure. Identify Lin as a blocker only if the actual clearance test establishes that fact. Presentation must not visually open walls, relocate occupants or imply guaranteed passage.",
      "learning": 0
    }
  ]
}

